      :class:`sympy.polys.fields.FracField` and keeps a reference to it as
      the ``field`` attribute.
    - For compatibility with older code the original coefficient domain is
      also available as the ``dom`` attribute (alias of ``domain``).

    Exceptions
    ----------
    Conversions performed by helpers may raise :class:`CoercionFailed` or
    :class:`GeneratorsError`. Some conversion helpers instead return ``None``
    to indicate an unsupported conversion path.
